# XSH flockfile(), ftrylockfile() and funlockfile()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.flockfile.001
anchor     functions/flockfile.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/flockfile.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       ftrylockfile() on a stream that no thread owns returns 0; after
           funlockfile(), ftrylockfile() called by another thread on the same
           stream also returns 0.
test       t/001-trylock-free.c

assertion  XSH.flockfile.002
anchor     functions/flockfile.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/flockfile.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       While the main thread owns a stream through flockfile(),
           ftrylockfile() called by another thread returns non-zero; after
           funlockfile() it returns 0.
test       t/002-owned-by-caller.c

assertion  XSH.flockfile.003
anchor     functions/flockfile.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       After three flockfile() calls by the main thread on one stream,
           ftrylockfile() by another thread returns non-zero after zero, one
           and two funlockfile() calls, and 0 after the third.
test       t/003-nested.c

assertion  XSH.flockfile.004
anchor     functions/flockfile.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       After a successful ftrylockfile() and then flockfile() by the main
           thread on one stream, ftrylockfile() by another thread returns
           non-zero after one funlockfile() call and 0 after the second.
test       t/004-trylock-nests.c

assertion  XSH.flockfile.005
anchor     functions/flockfile.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       While the main thread owns a stream, a second thread's flockfile()
           on it has not returned after 200 ms; once the main thread calls
           funlockfile() the second thread's call returns (within 10 s, else
           the result is UNRESOLVED).
timeout    70
test       t/005-flock-blocks.c

assertion  XSH.flockfile.006
anchor     functions/flockfile.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.5
class      required
says       While the main thread owns a stream opened "w+" through
           flockfile(), fputc('B') by a second thread has not returned after
           200 ms; after the main thread's fputc('A') and funlockfile() it
           returns, and rewind() then reads 'A' and 'B' in that order.
note       XSH 2.5 says every stdio function that reads or writes locks the
           stream as if by flockfile(); the page's APPLICATION USAGE says the
           owner blocks calls by other threads.
timeout    70
test       t/006-io-waits.c

assertion  XSH.flockfile.007
anchor     functions/flockfile.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       While the main thread owns one stream, ftrylockfile() by another
           thread on a second stream returns 0.
test       t/007-per-stream.c

assertion  XSH.flockfile.008
anchor     functions/flockfile.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.5
class      disputed
says       After flockfile() on a stream, ftrylockfile() by the same thread
           returns 0.
note       disputed (new: Q-79): the page calls ftrylockfile()
           the non-blocking version of flockfile(), which the owner may call
           again, and XSH 2.5 makes the lock reentrant, but the page states
           the count rule only for flockfile() and says ftrylockfile()
           acquires if the object is available; a FAIL is logged as INSPECT.
test       t/008-trylock-own.c
